#### Authorizations

clay-api-key

string

header

required

Personal API key tied to your Clay user. Create one under Settings → Account in the Clay app.

#### Body

application/json

Body

query

object

required

Show child attributes

cursor

string

Opaque cursor from the previous response. Scans page in least-recently-updated-first order and reflect concurrent writes: a record updated mid-scan can be returned again, so deduplicate by id.

limit

integer

default:50

Required range: `1 <= x <= 100`

#### Response

200

data

object[]

required

Show child attributes

cursor

string

fields

object

Show child attributes

truncated

boolean

True when more results matched than the limit but no cursor can be issued (grouped, aggregated, or custom-ordered queries do not support cursor pagination). Narrow the query or raise the limit to see the rest.

